  "worked_solution": "We factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any factors that they have in common.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4x-16y+4z}{20x-40z} & =\\frac{4(x-4y+z)}{20(x-2z)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{4}(x-4y+z)}{\\cancel{4}\\cdot 5(x-2z)} \\\\  & =\\frac{x-4y+z}{5x-10z}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
